※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4900

※ A requirement the types do not meet is reported at the **call**, by a note,
※ and at the requirement itself, which is what cannot be written.  That is the
※ whole of what a bound buys over checking the body per instantiation: the
※ message is about the signature a caller can read.

fn total(a: T', b: T') → T' pre(T' ⊞ T' → T'):
    a ⊞ b

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    ⎕narrow(total(true, false), ⌜u6⌝) ?? 1u6
